'\" t
.\" hydra-formats(1)
.TH HYDRA\-FORMATS 1 "2026-08-17" "hydra" "User Commands"
.
.SH NAME
hydra-formats \- list the file formats this build recognises
.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B hydra formats
.RI [ \-\-json ]
.RI [ \-\-category " NAME" ]
.RI [ \-\-what " NAME" ]
.
.SH DESCRIPTION
Prints the format catalogue this build classifies against, with a short
label and a one-sentence description for each.
Text by default;
.B \-\-json
emits the same catalogue for a GUI to render as tooltips or a type filter.
.PP
Classification is by the payload's
.B magic bytes,
not by the file extension and not by the server's
.BR Content\-Type .
Both of those are frequently wrong, and the project's own test corpus
contains a case where the documentation was wrong too: a page describing its
extensionless sample as MP4 serves a file whose magic bytes are FLV,
byte-identical to the FLV sample beside it.
Magic-byte precedence is what makes
.B "hydra \-y"
file that object correctly.
.PP
When the payload, the name, and the server's declared type disagree, the
disagreement is reported rather than resolved silently \(em as
.B format_conflict
in
.BR "hydra \-\-json" .
.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-json
Machine-readable output: an object with a
.B formats
array, each entry carrying
.BR format ,
.BR label ,
and
.BR description .
.TP
.BI \-\-category " NAME"
Show only one category.
One of
.BR video ,
.BR audio ,
.BR image ,
.BR archive ,
.BR document ,
.BR application ,
.BR "disk image" ,
.BR font ,
.BR data ,
.BR markup .
.TP
.BI \-\-what " NAME"
Describe one format or extension and exit, e.g.\&
.BR "hydra formats \-\-what tar.gz" .
A leading dot is accepted.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print help.
.
.SH CATEGORIES AND DIRECTORIES
Under
.BR "hydra \-y" / \-\-sort\-by\-type ,
each category maps to a destination subdirectory, following IDM's
convention:
.TS
tab(@) box;
lb lb
l  l .
Category@Directory
_
video@Video
audio@Music
image@Images
archive@Compressed
document@Documents
application@Programs
disk image@Images/Disk
font@Fonts
data@Data
markup@Web
(unrecognised)@Other
.TE
.
.SH EXIT STATUS
Always 0 for a well-formed invocation; 2 for an unrecognised argument.
.
.SH EXAMPLES
.RS 4
.nf
hydra formats
hydra formats \-\-category video
hydra formats \-\-what .mkv
hydra formats \-\-json | jq '.formats | length'
.fi
.RE
.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR hydra (1),
.BR file (1)
